WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_pat_171'), 'The suite has a session-scoped fixture that seeds a promo code, and the log of one run shows:

```python
@pytest.fixture(scope="session")
def promo(api):
    status, body = api.post("/promos", {"code": "QA-LUNCH", "percent": 10})
    ...
```

```text
[gw0] POST /promos 201
[gw1] POST /promos 409 code already exists
[gw2] POST /promos 409 code already exists
[gw3] POST /promos 409 code already exists
```

Statement: "With pytest-xdist every worker is its own process with its own test session, so a session-scoped fixture runs once per worker, here four times against the same API."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. pytest-xdist runs each worker as a separate Python process, and each one has its own session, so `scope="session"` means once per worker, not once per CI run. Four workers created the promo code four times, and three of them collided. Give the seeded data a per-worker name (the `worker_id` fixture), or create it once before the run (a CI step, or a file lock as the pytest-xdist docs describe).', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_pat_171') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
